## Exact source mechanism and minimal fix

Exact fixture `0686dcf7db39d385629b604860b907a2aa0e19f64d4766f83af83031c2a329c1` initializes each row with `generation:null` at598. At640 its validated serial enters `row.merge({"generation": int(serial), "format_version": wire.format_version})` without overwrite enabled. The existing null therefore survives, and645 evaluates `int(row.generation)` behind the stored-primary branch. The actual archived Store header is ordinary JSON format2/generation1, **not an Exact integer envelope**.

Godot documents `Dictionary.merge` with overwrite defaulting to false; existing keys are preserved. Direct assignment replaces the value. [Official Dictionary API](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_dictionary.html#class-dictionary-method-merge).

The minimal additive TEST correction is explicit assignment after the existing validated finite/integral/range/header check:

```gdscript
if parsed:
    row["generation"] = int(serial)
    row["format_version"] = wire["format_version"]
```

A narrow `row.get("generation") is int` guard followed by direct equality can make unexpected metadata a controlled custody refusal. Do not merely avoid the comparison or retain null, relax Store/header/stability/readback/ownership checks, rewrite raw bytes or change mechanics/setup/framing. Of the fixture’s three merges,619 adds new byte/hash/mtime keys and633 adds new archive keys; only640 overlaps an initialized key. The plain control sidecar constructs a new finite dictionary and uses no merge or native decoder.

